{"id": "EUVD-2026-107493", "enisaUuid": "851bafdd-bc9e-316f-a81a-4585cdd8c99d", "description": "Apache Traffic Server forwarded a malformed 302 response that should have been rejected as a parse error, because the Transfer-Encoding: chunked carve-out bypassed the rejection path. A response that two peers can read differently is then stored and served, allowing cache poisoning and response-framing desync.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Traffic Server: from 8.0.0 through 8.1.11, from 9.0.0 through 9.2.15, from 10.0.0 through 10.1.4, 10.2.0.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 9.2.16, 10.1.5, or 10.2.1, which fix the issue.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T18:26:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T18:26:32", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:L/SI:H/SA:N", "references": ["https://lists.apache.org/thread/r95dq29ywcd1f4x30snxlqmb12z4s4kc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111816", "GHSA-2g9h-67x8-9xr9"], "assigner": "apache", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "303ed8af-9a3e-330a-9039-ecfabefadd06", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "9.0.0 \u22649.2.15"}, {"id": "3ad9f414-0808-3e15-b93a-1a09e0470df2", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "8.0.0 \u22648.1.11"}, {"id": "64b23b78-048e-3041-8fec-9bcb5ef302ed", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "10.0.0 \u226410.1.4"}, {"id": "69de2af4-7529-3213-8757-781eadfac3eb", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "10.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "af1288c7-5c8a-3d33-b282-e14048597ee1", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}